  "id": "speaking-in-tongues",
  "term": "speaking in tongues",
  "definition": "Speaking in tongues, or glossolalia, is the rhythmic production of word-like speech that does not show stable meaning or usual sentence structure. In the source, it is described as a culturally rooted religious practice whose relationship to mental disorder remains debated rather than established.",
